  entry
    definition "something that bulges out or is protuberant or projects from its surroundings"
    examples ("the gun in his pocket made an obvious bulge" "the hump of a camel" "he stood on the rocky prominence" "the occipital protuberance was well developed" "the bony excrescence between its horns")
    id oewn-13917127-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (bulge hump swelling gibbosity gibbousness jut prominence protuberance protrusion extrusion excrescence)
  entry
    definition "an impact (as from a collision)"
    examples ("the bump threw him off the bicycle")
    id oewn-07353281-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (blow)
  entry
    definition "knock against with force or violence"
    examples ("My car bumped into the tree")
    id oewn-01242183-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (knock)
  entry
    definition "come upon, as if by accident; meet with"
    examples ("We find this idea in Plato" "I happened upon the most wonderful bakery not very far from here" "She chanced upon an interesting book in the bookstore the other day")
    id oewn-02253273-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (find happen chance encounter)
  entry
    definition "dance erotically or dance with the pelvis thrust forward"
    examples ("bump and grind")
